.TH LIDSLEEP 1 2026-09-16 "lidsleep 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lidsleep \- control whether closing the laptop lid suspends
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lidsleep
.RB { on | off | toggle }
.RB [ \-p | \-\-permanent ]
.br
.B lidsleep
.RB [ status | reset | help | version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lidsleep
turns lid close suspend on or off on systems using systemd-logind.
When lid sleep is off, the systemd user service
.I lidsleep.service
holds a
.B handle-lid-switch
inhibitor lock, so logind ignores the lid switch.
Nothing needs root.
.PP
Whether the service is enabled decides the default applied at each login.
Changes made without
.B \-\-permanent
only last until logout.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B on
Closing the lid suspends.
.TP
.B off
Closing the lid does nothing.
.TP
.B toggle
Switch between on and off.
.TP
.B status
Show the current setting and whether it is permanent.
This is the default when no command is given.
.TP
.B reset
Turn lid sleep back on, disable the service and remove the unit file
lidsleep wrote to the user's config directory, if any.
.TP
.B help
Show usage.
.TP
.B version
Show the version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-permanent
With
.BR on ,
.B off
or
.BR toggle ,
also save the new setting as the default for future logins.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/lidsleep.service
Written on first use when no packaged copy of the unit is installed.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/lidsleep.service
Unit installed by a package.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set, output is not colored.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure, 2 on bad usage.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd-inhibit (1),
.BR logind.conf (5)
